  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the national elections held in October 2026, no single political bloc in Israel succeeded in securing an outright majority in the legislature. This development led to a protracted period of coalition negotiations as various parties attempted to form a government. Gadi Eisenkot, the former military chief, has been actively negotiating with multiple political factions, including Yair Golan's Democrats party, to build a viable governing coalition to challenge Binyamin Netanyahu. These efforts come amid broader public and political discourse regarding the administration's management of security, including the recent conflict. Reports indicate that Eisenkot, previously known for a centrist military career, is now leveraging these alliances to consolidate opposition support. While previous reports noted a temporary halt in some discussions, the recent agreement marks a significant step in the ongoing power struggle to replace the current prime minister.",
